Ticket **#4471** merged **412** reports about wrong booking dates and was marked known as one
parser bug. Run through the kb's own cause rule (`causes.ts`), the merge holds **two causes**.

Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October: `parser` fixed by `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`,
`hint` won't fix because the booking-v3 form was retired.

<Callout>
[#3 parser · 379 reports](https://github.com/dawidLubcz/s01e03-what-it-shows-v2/issues/3): closed as completed (fixed).
[#4 hint · 33 reports](https://github.com/dawidLubcz/s01e03-what-it-shows-v2/issues/4): closed as not planned (won't fix).
</Callout>

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Filed tickets

| Cause | Reports | GitHub | Outcome | Belongs on #4471? |
|-------|--------:|--------|---------|-------------------|
| `parser` | **379** | [issue #3](https://github.com/dawidLubcz/s01e03-what-it-shows-v2/issues/3) | fixed | yes — month-first parser vs day-first tenants |
| `hint` | **33** | [issue #4](https://github.com/dawidLubcz/s01e03-what-it-shows-v2/issues/4) | won't fix | no — booking-v3 **MM/DD/YYYY** hint on day-first locales |

The `hint` reports were merged into #4471 before anyone split them. The parser fix did not
resolve them; retiring booking-v3 removed their cause.

## Lessons

- Count causes before you merge, not only subjects.
- Intake tags (`parser` / `hint`) are guesses; tenant locale and form version decide the cause.

